Verbatim transcript of originals/application_original.pdf — a two-page
scan of the existing paper rental application, with handwritten edit notes
on it.

The PDF has no text layer (two full-page images, no fonts), so this was
transcribed by reading the scan rather than extracted.

Printed text is reproduced as-is, including its errors. Several are
obvious ("Leasee", "his gents", "have e been given", a parenthesis that
never closes, a duplicated clause) — they are left exactly as printed,
the same rule the lease transcript follows: what the paper says is a
legal question, not a typo to autocorrect. They are listed at the end so
they are not mistaken for transcription slips.

Blanks are shown as ____ ; their length in the original is not
significant. Handwritten annotations are transcribed separately, after
each page, with their position on the page.

===============================================================================
